   "spoken": "The bishop to g5 is the Averbakh's sting. It means Black's natural e5 break now costs a pawn, because after the centre trades the pin on the knight on f6 tells — so Black is nudged into the slightly awkward h6.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "The Averbakh's bishop on g5 pre-empts Black's freeing e5 break by pinning the f6-knight.",
   "plans": "Provoke h6, retreat the bishop to e3, then storm with g4 and h4."
